                "text": "**Analyzing the Pattern**\n\nI've been analyzing the given training examples and focusing on the consistency of how the \"1\" elements are treated across the different input rows. It seems the output is maintaining the \"1\" values in the same positions, which is providing a good basis for understanding how the transformation logic works. I am currently examining the relationships of the values around the 1's as the values around the values change, to find patterns and rules.\n\n\n**Observing Shape Alignment**\n\nI'm now focused on the vertical alignment of the shapes. It looks like the \"4\" and \"2\" values shift downwards to align with the rows containing the \"1\" values. It seems the alignment happens by determining the row ranges for each shape, and all shapes align to match the \"1\" value. This shift keeps shapes aligned with the same row range of 1!\n\n\n**Investigating Vertical Alignment**\n\nI'm now deeply considering why the shapes are vertically aligned. I'm checking if shape \"1\" is the constant anchor or if the lowest shape serves as the reference. Example 1 shows \"1\" at rows 1..3, lower than rows 0..2. Example 3 has \"2\" and \"1\" at rows 2..4, lower than \"4\" at rows 0..2. I'm also considering a gravity-like effect, but questioning why the shapes stop mid-grid, and don't fall to the bottom.\n\n\n",
